            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DEO01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Tommaso</forename>
                        <surname>de Ocheda</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1757">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1831"/>
                    <occupation>librarian</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>De Ocheda was librarian to politician and book collector Lord George John Spencer (1758–1834) during the 1790s. 
    Spencer went on to amass the gretest private library in Europe. Prior to this de Ocheda was librarian to Pietro Antonio Crevenna (1726-92) 1785-9. Crevenna was obliged 
  to sell his important collection in 1789 for financial reasons which must have precipitated de Ocheda's departure.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">Michael Timko, 'Count Mac Carthy-Reagh and Bodoni', <title>The Book Collector</title>, 9:1 (Spring 1960), p. 72.</bibl>
